($q$Set Matrix Zeroes Warehouse Grid$q$,$q$set-matrix-zeroes$q$,$q$Medium$q$,$q$DSA$q$,ARRAY['arrays','matrix'],$q$## Problem

A Warehousing grid represents stock levels. If any cell is `0`, set its **entire row and column** to `0` in-place. Use O(1) extra space.$q$,$q$1 ≤ m,n ≤ 200 | -2^31 ≤ matrix[i][j] ≤ 2^31-1$q$,$q$[{"input": "matrix = [[1,1,1],[1,0,1],[1,1,1]]", "output": "[[1,0,1],[0,0,0],[1,0,1]]"}]$q$::jsonb,$q$[{"input": "[[1,1,1],[1,0,1],[1,1,1]]", "expected_output": "[[1,0,1],[0,0,0],[1,0,1]]", "is_hidden": false}, {"input": "[[0,1,2,0],[3,4,5,2],[1,3,1,5]]", "expected_output": "[[0,0,0,0],[0,4,5,0],[0,3,1,0]]", "is_hidden": true}]$q$::jsonb,$q$Use first row/col as markers. Two passes. O(m×n) time O(1) space.$q$,ARRAY['python','java','javascript','go','cpp'],0.55)
